   "source": [
    "# 06 - Multivariate Filter Feature Selection\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook performs the third classification experiment using a\n",
    "multivariate filter feature-selection strategy.\n",
    "\n",
    "Unlike the univariate approach, which evaluates each feature independently,\n",
    "the multivariate filter considers both:\n",
    "\n",
    "- The relevance of each feature with respect to the target variable.\n",
    "- The redundancy between the selected features.\n",
    "\n",
    "The same preprocessing strategy, classifiers, evaluation metrics, and\n",
    "cross-validation folds used in the previous experiments are maintained."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "id": "81a97aeb",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "\n",
    "from scipy import sparse\n",
    "\n",
    "from sklearn.base import BaseEstimator, TransformerMixin\n",
    "\n",
    "from sklearn.compose import ColumnTransformer\n",
    "from sklearn.preprocessing import OneHotEncoder, StandardScaler\n",
    "from sklearn.pipeline import Pipeline\n",
    "\n",
    "from sklearn.feature_selection import mutual_info_classif\n",
    "\n",
    "from sklearn.model_selection import (\n",
    "    StratifiedKFold,\n",
    "    cross_validate\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "from sklearn.neighbors import KNeighborsClassifier\n",
    "from sklearn.tree import DecisionTreeClassifier\n",
    "from sklearn.svm import SVC\n",
    "from sklearn.neural_network import MLPClassifier\n",
    "\n",
    "pd.set_option(\"display.max_columns\", None)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "24b92b28",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Dataset Preparation\n",
    "\n",
    "The same dataset preparation used in the previous experiments is maintained.\n",
    "\n",
    "Identifier and constant attributes are removed, while `Attrition` is encoded\n",
    "as a binary target:\n",
    "\n",
    "- `No` -> 0\n",
    "- `Yes` -> 1\n",
    "\n",
    "Keeping the dataset preparation unchanged ensures that differences in\n",
    "performance are attributable to the feature-selection strategy."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 2,
   "id": "7e5803f4",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Predictor matrix shape: (1470, 30)\n",
      "Target shape: (1470,)\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "DATA_PATH = \""../../data/raw/WA_Fn-UseC_-HR-Employee-Attrition.csv\"\n",
    "\n",
    "df = pd.read_csv(DATA_PATH)\n",
    "\n",
    "columns_to_remove = [\n",
    "    \"EmployeeNumber\",\n",
    "    \"EmployeeCount\",\n",
    "    \"Over18\",\n",
    "    \"StandardHours\"\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "df_model = df.drop(columns=columns_to_remove)\n",
    "\n",
    "X = df_model.drop(columns=[\"Attrition\"])\n",
    "\n",
    "y = df_model[\"Attrition\"].map({\n",
    "    \"No\": 0,\n",
    "    \"Yes\": 1\n",
    "})\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Predictor matrix shape:\", X.shape)\n",
    "print(\"Target shape:\", y.shape)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "d96bcaed",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Preprocessing Definition\n",
    "\n",
    "The same preprocessing strategy used in the baseline and univariate\n",
    "experiments is preserved.\n",
    "\n",
    "Numerical predictors are standardized and categorical predictors are\n",
    "one-hot encoded.\n",
    "\n",
    "The preprocessing transformer remains inside the machine-learning pipeline so\n",
    "that all transformations are learned exclusively from the training data of\n",
    "each cross-validation fold."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 3,
   "id": "6a5e061c",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Numerical predictors: 23\n",
      "Categorical predictors: 7\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "numerical_features = X.select_dtypes(\n",
    "    include=np.number\n",
    ").columns.tolist()\n",
    "\n",
    "categorical_features = X.select_dtypes(\n",
    "    exclude=np.number\n",
    ").columns.tolist()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Numerical predictors:\", len(numerical_features))\n",
    "print(\"Categorical predictors:\", len(categorical_features))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 4,
   "id": "b1436a58",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "preprocessor = ColumnTransformer(\n",
    "    transformers=[\n",
    "        (\n",
    "            \"num\",\n",
    "            StandardScaler(),\n",
    "            numerical_features\n",
    "        ),\n",
    "        (\n",
    "            \"cat\",\n",
    "            OneHotEncoder(handle_unknown=\"ignore\"),\n",
    "            categorical_features\n",
    "        )\n",
    "    ]\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "76e1a285",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Multivariate Filter Feature Selection\n",
    "\n",
    "A multivariate filter should evaluate features not only according to their\n",
    "individual relationship with the target, but also according to the information\n",
    "they provide when considered together.\n",
    "\n",
    "A relevance-redundancy strategy inspired by Minimum Redundancy Maximum\n",
    "Relevance (mRMR) is used in this experiment.\n",
    "\n",
    "The method follows two principles:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Maximum relevance:** selected features should contain information about\n",
    "  the target variable.\n",
    "- **Minimum redundancy:** selected features should avoid providing highly\n",
    "  duplicated information.\n",
    "\n",
    "Feature relevance is estimated using mutual information with the target.\n",
    "Redundancy is estimated using the absolute correlation between candidate\n",
    "features and the features already selected.\n",
    "\n",
    "The method is independent of the classification algorithm and therefore\n",
    "constitutes a filter-based feature-selection approach."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 5,
   "id": "3914ea1b",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "class MRMRSelector(BaseEstimator, TransformerMixin):\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    Greedy multivariate filter inspired by mRMR.\n",
    "\n",
    "    Features are selected by maximizing target relevance while\n",
    "    penalizing redundancy with features already selected.\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "\n",
    "    def __init__(\n",
    "        self,\n",
    "        k=15,\n",
    "        random_state=42\n",
    "    ):\n",
    "        self.k = k\n",
    "        self.random_state = random_state\n",
    "\n",
    "    def fit(self, X, y):\n",
    "\n",
    "        # Convert sparse matrices generated by one-hot encoding to dense arrays.\n",
    "        if sparse.issparse(X):\n",
    "            X_array = X.toarray()\n",
    "        else:\n",
    "            X_array = np.asarray(X)\n",
    "\n",
    "        n_features = X_array.shape[1]\n",
    "\n",
    "        if self.k > n_features:\n",
    "            raise ValueError(\n",
    "                \"k cannot be greater than the number of features.\"\n",
    "            )\n",
    "\n",
    "        # Measure the relevance of every feature with respect to the target.\n",
    "        relevance = mutual_info_classif(\n",
    "            X_array,\n",
    "            y,\n",
    "            random_state=self.random_state\n",
    "        )\n",
    "\n",
    "        # Correlation matrix used to quantify redundancy.\n",
    "        correlation = np.corrcoef(\n",
    "            X_array,\n",
    "            rowvar=False\n",
    "        )\n",
    "\n",
    "        correlation = np.nan_to_num(\n",
    "            np.abs(correlation),\n",
    "            nan=0.0\n",
    "        )\n",
    "\n",
    "        selected = []\n",
    "\n",
    "        # Start with the most relevant feature.\n",
    "        first_feature = int(np.argmax(relevance))\n",
    "        selected.append(first_feature)\n",
    "\n",
    "        # Greedily add features with high relevance and low redundancy.\n",
    "        while len(selected) < self.k:\n",
    "\n",
    "            best_feature = None\n",
    "            best_score = -np.inf\n",
    "\n",
    "            for feature in range(n_features):\n",
    "\n",
    "                if feature in selected:\n",
    "                    continue\n",
    "\n",
    "                redundancy = np.mean(\n",
    "                    correlation[feature, selected]\n",
    "                )\n",
    "\n",
    "                score = (\n",
    "                    relevance[feature]\n",
    "                    - redundancy\n",
    "                )\n",
    "\n",
    "                if score > best_score:\n",
    "                    best_score = score\n",
    "                    best_feature = feature\n",
    "\n",
    "            selected.append(best_feature)\n",
    "\n",
    "        self.selected_indices_ = np.array(selected)\n",
    "        self.relevance_scores_ = relevance\n",
    "\n",
    "        return self\n",
    "\n",
    "    def transform(self, X):\n",
    "\n",
    "        return X[:, self.selected_indices_]\n",
    "\n",
    "    def get_support(self):\n",
    "\n",
    "        return self.selected_indices_"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c55d559c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Number of Selected Features\n",
    "\n",
    "The multivariate filter retains 15 transformed features.\n",
    "\n",
    "The same number of features used in the univariate experiment is maintained\n",
    "to make the comparison between both feature-selection strategies more direct."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 6,
   "id": "ee0a1b67",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Number of transformed features to retain: 15\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "N_SELECTED_FEATURES = 15\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\n",
    "    f\"Number of transformed features to retain: \"\n",
    "    f\"{N_SELECTED_FEATURES}\"\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "d98b79b2",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Evaluation Strategy\n",
    "\n",
    "The same stratified 10-fold cross-validation procedure used in the previous\n",
    "experiments is maintained.\n",
    "\n",
    "For each cross-validation fold:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Preprocessing is fitted using only the training data.\n",
    "2. Feature relevance and redundancy are estimated using only the training data.\n",
    "3. The multivariate filter selects 15 transformed features.\n",
    "4. The classifier is trained using the selected features.\n",
    "5. The learned transformations and selected subset are applied to the\n",
    "   validation fold.\n",
    "6. Performance is measured exclusively on the validation fold.\n",
    "\n",
    "This ensures an honest evaluation and prevents information leakage during\n",
    "feature selection."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 7,
   "id": "1de68dba",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "cv = StratifiedKFold(\n",
    "    n_splits=10,\n",
    "    shuffle=True,\n",
    "    random_state=42\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "bdcd55a1",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. Evaluation Metrics\n",
    "\n",
    "The same metrics used in the previous experiments are maintained:\n",
    "\n",
    "- Accuracy\n",
    "- Precision\n",
    "- Recall\n",
    "- F1-score\n",
    "- Balanced Accuracy\n",
    "\n",
    "Particular attention is given to recall, F1-score, and balanced accuracy due\n",
    "to the imbalance of the target variable."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 8,
   "id": "cced92f5",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "scoring = {\n",
    "    \"accuracy\": \"accuracy\",\n",
    "    \"precision\": \"precision\",\n",
    "    \"recall\": \"recall\",\n",
    "    \"f1\": \"f1\",\n",
    "    \"balanced_accuracy\": \"balanced_accuracy\"\n",
    "}"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a3799dd0",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 7. Classification Algorithms\n",
    "\n",
    "The same classifier configurations used in the baseline and univariate\n",
    "experiments are maintained.\n",
    "\n",
    "This ensures that the multivariate feature-selection strategy is the only\n",
    "experimental factor that changes."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 9,
   "id": "2cb06a60",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "models = {\n",
    "    \"K-NN\": KNeighborsClassifier(),\n",
    "\n",
    "    \"Decision Tree\": DecisionTreeClassifier(\n",
    "        random_state=42\n",
    "    ),\n",
    "\n",
    "    \"SVM\": SVC(),\n",
    "\n",
    "    \"Neural Network\": MLPClassifier(\n",
    "        random_state=42,\n",
    "        max_iter=2000\n",
    "    )\n",
    "}"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "803f02f3",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 8. Evaluation Function\n",
    "\n",
    "For each classifier, preprocessing, multivariate feature selection, and\n",
    "classification are combined into a single scikit-learn `Pipeline`.\n",
    "\n",
    "Consequently, the feature subset is selected independently inside every\n",
    "training fold."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 11,
   "id": "e333ecaf",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def evaluate_model(\n",
    "    name,\n",
    "    classifier,\n",
    "    X,\n",
    "    y,\n",
    "    cv,\n",
    "    scoring\n",
    "):\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    Evaluate a classifier using preprocessing,\n",
    "    multivariate filter feature selection,\n",
    "    and stratified cross-validation.\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "\n",
    "    pipeline = Pipeline(\n",
    "        steps=[\n",
    "            (\"preprocessing\", preprocessor),\n",
    "            (\n",
    "                \"feature_selection\",\n",
    "                MRMRSelector(\n",
    "                    k=N_SELECTED_FEATURES,\n",
    "                    random_state=42\n",
    "                )\n",
    "            ),\n",
    "            (\"classifier\", classifier)\n",
    "        ]\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "    scores = cross_validate(\n",
    "        pipeline,\n",
    "        X,\n",
    "        y,\n",
    "        cv=cv,\n",
    "        scoring=scoring,\n",
    "        n_jobs=-1\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "    result = {\n",
    "        \"Model\": name,\n",
    "        \"Selected Features\": N_SELECTED_FEATURES\n",
    "    }\n",
    "\n",
    "    for metric in scoring.keys():\n",
    "\n",
    "        metric_values = scores[f\"test_{metric}\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "        result[f\"{metric}_mean\"] = metric_values.mean()\n",
    "        result[f\"{metric}_std\"] = metric_values.std()\n",
    "\n",
    "    return result"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "390408b0",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 9. Model Evaluation\n",
    "\n",
    "Each classifier is evaluated after applying multivariate filter feature\n",
    "selection.\n",
    "\n",
    "The same number of selected features, evaluation folds, preprocessing\n",
    "operations, and metrics are used for every classifier."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 12,
   "id": "ef10822f",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Evaluating K-NN...\n",
      "Evaluating Decision Tree...\n",
      "Evaluating SVM...\n",
      "Evaluating Neural Network...\n",
      "\n",
      "Evaluation completed.\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "results = []\n",
    "\n",
    "for name, model in models.items():\n",
    "\n",
    "    print(f\"Evaluating {name}...\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    result = evaluate_model(\n",
    "        name=name,\n",
    "        classifier=model,\n",
    "        X=X,\n",
    "        y=y,\n",
    "        cv=cv,\n",
    "        scoring=scoring\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "    results.append(result)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nEvaluation completed.\")"
   ]
  },
