  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e5141ef9",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 15. Main Observations\n",
    "\n",
    "The multivariate filter reduces the transformed representation from 51\n",
    "features to 15 selected features while considering both relevance to the\n",
    "target and redundancy between predictors.\n",
    "\n",
    "The effect of the multivariate selection differs across classifiers:\n",
    "\n",
    "- The **Neural Network** achieves the best multivariate-filter performance,\n",
    "  with an F1-score of 0.3902 and a balanced accuracy of 0.6341.\n",
    "\n",
    "- The **Decision Tree** performs similarly, obtaining an F1-score of 0.3748\n",
    "  and a balanced accuracy of 0.6306.\n",
    "\n",
    "- The **K-NN** classifier performs worse than in both the baseline and\n",
    "  univariate experiments. Its F1-score decreases to 0.1632 and its recall\n",
    "  falls to 0.1018.\n",
    "\n",
    "- The **SVM** is particularly affected by the selected subset. Although its\n",
    "  accuracy remains relatively high (0.8442), its recall drops to 0.0511 and\n",
    "  its F1-score to 0.0910, showing that it identifies very few employees in the\n",
    "  attrition class.\n",
    "\n",
    "- Compared with the univariate filter, the multivariate strategy slightly\n",
    "  improves the Neural Network but reduces the performance of K-NN and SVM.\n",
    "  The Decision Tree remains relatively stable.\n",
    "\n",
    "- Compared with the baseline using all features, none of the classifiers\n",
    "  improves overall. The Neural Network baseline remains the strongest result\n",
    "  according to F1-score and balanced accuracy.\n",
    "\n",
    "- The multivariate selector avoids selecting both complementary dummy\n",
    "  variables of `OverTime`. It retains `OverTime_Yes` while excluding\n",
    "  `OverTime_No`, illustrating the intended redundancy-reduction behaviour.\n",
    "\n",
    "- Several highly relevant variables such as `JobLevel`, `Age`,\n",
    "  `TotalWorkingYears`, and `YearsAtCompany` are not selected despite having\n",
    "  non-negligible relevance scores. This occurs because the multivariate\n",
    "  criterion also penalizes redundancy with features already included in the\n",
    "  subset.\n",
    "\n",
    "Overall, the multivariate filter produces a more diverse and less redundant\n",
    "subset of features, but this does not translate into better predictive\n",
    "performance than the original feature representation."
   ]
  }
